Z||000000||maryjane||08-08-2001||09:55 PM||||There have been a lot of posts with some really hard to pin down problems since I've been reading PFF. Not just the usual "bad idle , running like crap-turned out to be 02 sensor" thing, but the really hard to find a fix for problems. If you get a problem solved, try to go back and find your original post and let everyone know what you did to fix it. (a lot of members do this now, but a lot don't). It can save the next person a lot of time, money, & aggravation, plus, makes doing a search thru the archives a lot more productive. I've seen posts with major headaches and lots of suggestions, the post fades away without resolution and the next post by that same person; it's like nothing ever happened.We all like to hear happy endings too. Thanks<BR>Don||||reg||1
